# Normalise our own sources to LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Last match wins, so these override the rule above.
#
# Vendored third-party code must keep its exact bytes: the SHA-256 integrity
# digests in README.md and reference/PROVENANCE.md are computed over the working
# tree with `find | sort | xargs cat | sha256sum`, and four of the shipped Sesame
# files legitimately contain CRLF.
reference/** -text

# Generated results are evidence: keep them byte-stable across platforms so that
# recomputed metrics and archived per-point CSVs match on any clone.
data/** -text
figures/** -text
